>> title: Sunomono
>> category: Salads
>> tags: japanese, cucumber, wakame, vinegar, side, no-cook, quick
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: 酢の物, sunomono, sunomono, すのもの, きゅうりとわかめの酢の物, kyuri to wakame no sunomono, cucumber and wakame salad, vinegared cucumber
>> pairs-with: gohan, saba-no-misoni
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: narrow — a cucumber that has not been salted and wrung out keeps giving up water, and within the hour the dressing is thin and tastes only of sugar; salted properly it holds a day, and the vinegar cannot be cut back to compensate without the whole thing going flat
>> step.1: The vinegar ratio is the recipe. 三杯酢 — vinegar 3 : sugar 2 : soy 1 — and everything else here is preparation for it.
>> step.2: salt, draw 10 min, wring out
>> step.3: soak 8 min
>> step.4: whisk and dress
>> step.5: chill 15 min

The vinegar ratio is the recipe. 三杯酢 is vinegar 3 : sugar 2 : soy 1, the standard three-part dressing, and everything else in this file is preparation for it.

Salt @cucumbers{2}(Japanese or Persian, sliced as thin as you can) with @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp} in a #bowl{} and leave them ~draw{10%min}, until a pool has collected, then wring them out a handful at a time.

Soak @dried wakame{2%Tbs}(5 g) in @cold water{}(a bowlful) ~soak{8%min}, until it has opened out and gone deep green, then drain it and chop any long pieces.

Whisk @rice vinegar{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @sugar{2%Tbs} and @soy sauce{1%Tbs}(15 mL) until the sugar has gone, and turn @&(2)wrung cucumber{} and @&(~1)wakame{} through it.

Chill @&(~1)sunomono{} ~chill{15%min} with @grated ginger{1%tsp} stirred through, and drain off whatever has collected before it goes to the table.
